By the 4 October 2026 export, **412 unique reports** about wrong booking dates had been merged
into #4471. The export has 427 rows: 15 report IDs appear twice because its pages overlap, so
each report must be counted once.

Those reports do not share one cause. The largest group is a shared parser that reads dates
month first for tenants who write dates day first. A second group comes only from booking-v3
forms: their month-first hint conflicts with those tenants' day-first locale. The table uses
the tenant directory, channel and form to classify reports; the intake tag is only a guess.

<Callout>
Known, but split the work: 379 reports point to the shared parser; 33 point to the booking-v3
date hint. Fixing one does not fix the other.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The parser group spans all 11 tenants and app, email and booking-v2 form reports. The hint group
contains 33 booking-v3 form reports from three tenants. Intake mislabeled 38 reports: 23 parser
reports were tagged `hint`, and 15 hint reports were tagged `parser`. Five one-day-move reports
in the desk notes remain in the parser group; the symptom alone does not establish a third cause.

## GitHub tickets

- [Shared parser · 379 reports](https://github.com/Kowalskiexe/mega-dev-2137/issues/1)
- [booking-v3 date hint · 33 reports](https://github.com/Kowalskiexe/mega-dev-2137/issues/2)

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- Deduplicate by report ID before counting; overlapping export pages repeat records.
- Classify from tenant locale, channel and form, not subject wording or the intake tag.
- Treat these counts as an export snapshot: the desk keeps receiving reports after 4 October.
